/whizark/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whizark/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whizark/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whizark/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whizark/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whizark/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whizark/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whizark/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-07-16T19:43:47Z","updated_at":"2016-07-16T19:43:47Z","body":"@btmills Thank you for you explanation.  I had a slight misunderstanding about _align_... :flushed: \nI tried to lint the first code in [align and multiLine](https://github.com/eslint/eslint/blob/67c3cc2fa655e9e92e01d7a88e9a9d60cd4a4ce9/docs/rules/key-spacing.md#align-and-multiline) with `case1.js` config and the code actually passed, so I also tried to lint another code based on the code above.\n\n``` javascript\nvar myObj = {\n  key1: 1, // uses multiLine\n\n  key2:    2, // uses align (when defined)\n  key3:    3, // uses align (when defined)\n\n  key4: 4 // uses multiLine\n}\n```\n\nThe result is:\n\n``` shell\n  4:12  error  Extra space before value for key 'key2'  key-spacing\n  5:12  error  Extra space before value for key 'key3'  key-spacing\n```\n\nI'm a little confused because `multiLine.align.mode`  in `case1.js` seems to be overridden with `multiLine.mode`. Is this also a bug? Or we cannot use both `multiLine.mode` and `multiLine.align.mode` in the same time?\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/233147515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"whizark","id":1211058,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTEwNTg=","avatar